WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.200
Why does this matter?

2
00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:05.883
The Zero Trust Assessment tests a tenant
against hundreds of configuration

3
00:00:05.883 --> 00:00:10.712
items from Microsoft's guidance for Entra,
Intune, Azure networking and Purview.

4
00:00:10.712 --> 00:00:14.291
Release three point one point
oh, the current release,

5
00:00:14.291 --> 00:00:17.950
holds three hundred sixty-four
tests in seven pillars.

6
00:00:17.950 --> 00:00:19.360
It's read-only, it's free,

7
00:00:19.360 --> 00:00:23.825
and it's the assessment component
of Microsoft's Zero Trust Workshop.

8
00:00:23.825 --> 00:00:26.537
The report is accurate on the day it runs.

9
00:00:26.537 --> 00:00:29.693
What it doesn't do is tell
you what a skipped test means,

10
00:00:29.693 --> 00:00:32.275
what to fix first, or
when a finding is closed.

11
00:00:32.275 --> 00:00:34.456
Those are decisions for named people,

12
00:00:34.456 --> 00:00:37.200
and the report is the
evidence they decide with.

13
00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:41.040
That's the title of this
module: evidence, not a verdict.
